Z||000000||DisfourDan||05-25-2001||06:40 PM||||I told a few friends I was going to get a Fiero, and they laughed at the thought.  Just wondering, why did the Fiero get such a bad rap?<P>------------------<BR>Nothing good can come from good.||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||05-25-2001||07:03 PM||||Wow, that's a tale often told. I must admit, I once scoffed at Fieros myself. That was before I actually drove one. There was a lot of hype when the Fiero first came out, to be followed by the inevitable backlash. To be honest and ubiased, the Fiero is far from a "no compromises" design. Plus the vast majority of Fieros that I see are tired pieces of crap. However,that can be said about any car not properly maintained.<P>It comes down to this, if you really care what other people think about what you drive, join the pack and get the latest trendy mobile.  If you want to drive a car with the best dollars to fun ratio, get a Fiero and f*ck the nay-sayers! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||05-25-2001||07:23 PM||||Well said Stimpy!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Urchin||05-25-2001||07:30 PM||||Agreed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_8.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||sjp777||05-25-2001||07:51 PM||||Happens all the time. When ever people ask what kind of car I have and I answer "a Fiero" I get a look that's a little too much like pity. Until they see it of course, then all they can seem to say is "Wow"<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||12
Z||000005||frontal lobe||05-25-2001||07:55 PM||||Lots of reasons.  Some deserved.  '84 Fiero's had a disturbing propensity to have engine fires.  They looked very sporty and a lot of people didn't think the 4 cylinder delivered what the looks were suggesting.  The car has been discontinued so easy to claim as obsolete.  Main reason-most have never driven one.<P>So if you want your car to be a status-symbol in any way, you should probably get another car because it will be poorly respected by the general population.<P>If you want a relatively light weight, zippy, fun to drive car that has body panels that aren't going to rust out, and will have lots of replacement parts available for a car it's age, get it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DisfourDan||05-25-2001||10:11 PM||||I could care less of what people say, and there little remarks made no dent in my armor.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||AusFiero||05-26-2001||11:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DisfourDan:<BR><B>I could care less of what people say, and there little remarks made no dent in my armor.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats the spirit Dan. I suppose you have heard it  all anyway with driving a Volvo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
