Z||000011||camaro2fiero||05-27-2001||03:00 AM||||When I sold my 69  plain jane camaro . I bought my 84 Fiero.My friends kept telling me that I should not buy a Fiero.I kept hearing the same old stuff,Didnt they catch on fire,etc,etc.Well I think that this car is the best car I have owned.Its funny how all kinds of cars seem to want to race my little 4 cyl.I do want to buy a Fastback so how much is too much.A car lot up the road has a 87 for 5000. V6 in nice condition.But I want to get my 84 squared away first. Suspension and other things.||||reg||6
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||05-27-2001||11:53 AM||||Wanna really mess up some peoples heads - take all the Fiero markings and Pontaic markings off your car <P>  then when someone asks you what kinda car it is, tell them:<P>  1. Its a prototype my uncle made, was planning on starting his own production company, but capitol investors fell through at the last minute. He only made 3, this is the last one.<P>   2. It the first prototpe of the Saturn - but they decided to go with a 4 passenger car instead (good if your car looks 10 years old)<P>   3. Its a new saturn prototype - will be out next year, maybe - thats all Im allowed to say (good if your car looks like new).<P>   4. Its a car we made at RPI, MIT, RIT, UCLA (insert your favorite school name here) for a national engineering design contest - we took second place - each of the students that helped design the car get to use it for 6 months now on a rotating schedule. Then show them the air intake plenium or some other cool part of the car and say, "this is the part I designed"<P>   You can have a lot of fun with this, make up details of what factors were used to judge the contest - there was a 300 mile race on the indy track... best fuel economy, best 1/4 mile times...<P>5. ?<P>   You can have a lot of fun with a car that has no manufactures markings on it. Esp if someone has never seen one before. An 18 year old kid was 5 when they stopped making Fieros.||||reg||1
