Z||000014||Ed||05-27-2001||05:43 PM||||Hey FierobearRoadtrip:<P>There's a club in Sacramento.  Golden Gate is a good club, but we're about 100 miles closer to you!  Please e-mail me for info. <P>Or join us too, and Classic Fiero Owners' Group.  You can belong to three clubs in northern California!   <P>Ed, President<BR>Northern CA Chpt., FOCOA||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierosound||05-27-2001||06:44 PM||||When I told my friends I bought a Fiero, none actually laughed.  But when I showed up with an 87 GT they asked "That's a Fiero?" and were blown away by it.  Seems most people think of the original 84 coupe when you mention Fiero, along with the problems that model had.||||reg||10
Z||000016||FieroJoe||05-27-2001||07:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierosound:<BR><B>Seems most people think of the original 84 coupe when you mention Fiero, along with the problems that model had.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I second that!  People remember that style/model because it was it's first year, and the fires gave it the most publicity, so they remember probably seeing a red 84 2m4 on the news or something.<P>Another thing I get is that noboby believes me that my color is factory.  Even a few of my teachers have said "They didnt make those in blue".  And then I start on my dissertaition that they only offered bright blue metallic in 87, 4,434 (around that #) made that color, and on and on...<P>Bascially, they dont challenge me on anything related to Fieros after I give them that speech!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
